<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · movement</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gandhara art</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Gandharan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gandhara art is a style of Buddhist art that developed in the region of Gandhara in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>. It combined Greek sculptural traditions, inherited from the Greek kingdoms that followed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a> in the east, with Buddhist subjects, and produced some of the earliest human images of the Buddha.</p></div>
